  "img": "systems/draw-steel/assets/classes/operator.png",
  "system": {
    "description": {
      "value": "<p>You are the crew's <strong>ghost in the machine</strong> - a force-multiplying net-controller who wins fights without firing a shot. You reach into the <strong>Wired</strong> (the unified Matrix layer running the lit world), breach its <strong>nodes</strong>, and turn the environment and the enemy's own gear against them: blind cameras, seize turrets, jam smartlinks, hijack drones, spoof doors. Your power flows from <strong>Bandwidth</strong>: intrusion throughput, never bought with nuyen or Body Integrity - earned only by getting deep and clean into the system. Corp records file you as a <em>security-penetration auditor</em>; the street calls you Null, the Grey Ghost.</p><h3>Bandwidth - the intrusion-momentum (breach-and-build) engine</h3><p>Starting pool and cap <strong>6</strong> at Tier 5 (the cap rises +3 per tier -> 9 / 12 / 15 / 18). Your first jack-in each encounter grants Bandwidth equal to your <strong>Victories</strong>. Gain <strong>+2</strong> whenever you breach a new node <em>or</em> land an Outcome Tier 1 on any Wired roll. At the start of each of your turns gain <strong>+1 per hostile node you hold compromised</strong>, up to a cap of <strong>4</strong> at Tier 5. Gain <strong>+1</strong> whenever a Wired action raises no Alert. All unspent Bandwidth is lost at encounter end - you jack out and the buffer clears. Signatures cost no Bandwidth; heroic abilities and Spend X enhancements drain it.</p><h3>Alert-master</h3><p>Alone in the crew you own the heat clock: Tier-2/Tier-3 Wired results raise the Alert track, but you scrub it, mask your intrusions, and (via Total Intrusion) freeze it for the whole crew. Where everyone else fears rising Alert, you run it.</p><h3>Signatures &amp; Subclass</h3><p>Three signatures cost no Bandwidth: <strong>Intrusion</strong> (your core Cognition Power Roll), <strong>Subvert</strong>, and <strong>Electronic Warfare</strong>. At Tier 5 you choose a subclass - the <strong>Disruptor (Offensive Decker)</strong> - which colors your signatures and grants an identity feature.</p><h3>Fragility &amp; Chrome</h3><p>The lowest Stamina in the crew; while jacked-in your body is inert and exposed, so the crew guards the meat while the mind is away. Chrome-positive (no Veil): your power runs through a datajack and combat-deck interface, so Body Integrity is pure upside.</p><h3>Advancement (internal Level 1-5 = player-facing Tier 5-1)</h3><p>At <strong>Tier 5</strong> you choose your subclass, gain all three signatures, and pick an opening heroic ability. Every Tier after, you gain a new heroic ability and your Bandwidth cap rises. The ladder caps at <strong>Tier 1</strong>.</p>",
      "director": ""
    },
